+// nothing but the card's dress -- the fill and rim painted here, the halo a
+// child (HeliumCardShadowView cuts the card out of itself, so above the fill
+// it only lands outside) -- fading as one.
+// ⛔ r1028: no layer of its own. A child's layer sits above everything its
+// parent paints itself -- the layerless siblings included -- whatever the
+// child's index: r1027 gave the dress a layer "at the bottom of the stack",
+// and the top row's buttons (layerless ToolbarButtons) went under its opaque
+// fill on the first frame and came back only as it faded (the user's
+// 10:58:56 recording, f_00257-f_00262; in the probe's own recording the one
+// button AXPress had just pressed, holding an ink-drop layer, was the one
+// that stayed). Layerless at index 0 it is the first thing drawn into the
+// region's layer, under every child; its fade is a save-layer alpha here,
+// and the halo's own layer takes the same alpha (SetShadowOpacity).
